# Cyber Threat Intelligence Agent - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is a Cyber Threat Intelligence (CTI) Agent built for a portfolio project targeting defense/intelligence roles at firms like Booz Allen Hamilton, Leidos, and MITRE. The agent researches cyber threats and produces structured threat briefs for analysts.

## Developer Profile
- Computer Science + Cybersecurity double major (senior, graduating May 2027)
- Beginner-to-intermediate Python level - explain concepts clearly and do not skip steps
- Background in ML/AI research (NASA anomaly detection, edge AI, computer vision)
- Learning agentic AI, RAG, and LLM APIs actively via DataCamp
- Goal: build a polished GitHub project to showcase at Booz Allen interviews

## Tech Stack
- Language: Python 3.10+
- LLM: Claude API (Anthropic) - model: claude-opus-4-20250514
- Agent framework: LangChain
- Web search: DuckDuckGo (via langchain-community)
- Vector DB (Part 3): ChromaDB
- API layer (Part 4): FastAPI
- Frontend (Part 4, optional): Streamlit
- Environment: Cursor IDE, virtual environment (`venv`)

