## Build Phases
- Part 1 (current): Core Agent
  - Set up environment, API keys, LangChain
  - Build agent loop with Claude API
  - Add DuckDuckGo web search tool
- Part 2 (current): Structured Output
  - Define JSON threat brief schema
  - Prompt engineering for consistent output
- Part 3 (after RAG DataCamp courses): RAG Integration
  - ChromaDB vector store
  - Ingest threat intelligence PDFs
  - Retrieval-augmented generation
- Part 4 (week 5-6): FastAPI Interface
  - REST endpoint for threat queries
  - Streamlit frontend (optional)
- Part 5: GitHub and Documentation
  - Clean README, demo GIF, deployment notes

## Coding Standards
- Always use `python-dotenv` to load API keys from `.env`; never hardcode keys
- Never commit `.env` files or secrets
- Add clear comments explaining what each function does and why
- Use descriptive variable names; readability matters for portfolio quality
- Handle errors gracefully with `try/except` and helpful error messages
- Keep functions small and focused: one function, one job
- Print progress updates so users can see the agent is working

## How Cursor Should Help
- Explain code in plain English when asked
- Walk through setup steps one at a time; do not skip steps
- When suggesting fixes, explain why the fix works
- Point out portfolio improvements (for example, what would present better on GitHub)
- Remind that `.env` files should never be committed
- Suggest variable names and comments that match defense/cyber domain language

## Key Terminology
- CTI = Cyber Threat Intelligence
- IoC = Indicator of Compromise
- TTPs = Tactics, Techniques, and Procedures
- MITRE ATT&CK = threat behavior framework used in defense/government
- Threat actor = hacker group or nation-state attacker
- Threat brief = structured analyst report on a specific threat
- RAG = Retrieval Augmented Generation
- Agentic AI = AI that plans and uses tools autonomously
